Backend tests issue real requests against the Hono app with real D1, R2, and KV via @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers. No unit tests of domain functions. No mocking of external libraries — not better-auth, not Drizzle, not the Workers runtime.

Port substitution is permitted for failure paths ONLY. No HTTP request can make R2 presigning throw or a queue send fail, so those branches are otherwise unreachable. Substituting an implementation of our own port that returns an error is exercising our contract, not faking someone else's library.

    // allowed — provoking an unreachable failure branch
    const failingStorage: ObjectStorage = { ...real, presignPut: async () => err({ kind: 'storage_unavailable' }) }

    // NOT allowed — substituting for convenience on a happy path
    const fakeRepo: ApplicationRepo = { findById: async () => ok(fixture) }

A substituted port on a happy path is a rule violation and will be rejected in review.

Fixtures in test/fixtures/ are first-class code, maintained with the same care as src/. HTTP-level tests are only writable if seeding is easy.

Frontend mirrors this with Playwright, also at 100%.

See docs/codebase-structure.md §13.
